Design inspiration

The policy model of HaltSQL (a declarative policy file, a
verify(sql, policy, context) entry point, machine-readable violation reasons,
and an HTTP sidecar) is inspired by the sql-guardrail project, which is
distributed under the MIT License. HaltSQL is an independent implementation:
it ports the design, not the code. Any test cases adapted from sql-guardrail
are attributed in the files that contain them and remain under the MIT License.

