Third-party software

HaltSQL parses SQL with libpg_query 17-6.2.5
(https://github.com/pganalyze/libpg_query), which is vendored in
vendor/libpg_query and bound by HaltSQL's own C stubs in lib/pgquery.
libpg_query is Copyright (c) 2015, Lukas Fittl, and Copyright (c) 2016-2023,
Duboce Labs, Inc. (pganalyze), distributed under the BSD 3-Clause License.
libpg_query contains source code extracted from PostgreSQL 17, Copyright (c)
1996-2024, The PostgreSQL Global Development Group, and Copyright (c) 1994,
The Regents of the University of California, distributed under the PostgreSQL
License. The full license texts are in vendor/libpg_query/LICENSE and are
included in every binary release.

Other dependencies (yojson, yaml, digestif, cmdliner, cohttp, lwt and their
transitive dependencies) are distributed under their own licenses. A
CycloneDX SBOM listing every component is attached to each release.
